AndChamber also contains app-local transport and stream-reader patches in the LibADB package,
app/src/main/java/io/github/muntashirakon/adb/AndChamberAdbTransport.kt and
AndChamberAdbStreamReader.kt, derived from LibADB Android 3.1.1 under its Apache-2.0 option with
the applicable BSD-3-Clause notices. They reuse the library's SPAKE2 cipher with bounded,
cancellable sockets, enforce TLS-only connections and correctly drain queued data before EOF.
The exact modifications, source URLs, the
Apache-2.0/LGPL-3.0/GPL-3.0/BSD-3-Clause/Bouncy Castle texts and the rebuild/relink instructions are
in third_party/phone-adb/ and packaged under assets/licenses/phone-adb/.

The license texts for the native components are in third_party/native-runtime/ (packaged under
assets/licenses/native/); the Java/Kotlin component texts are in third_party/phone-adb/ (packaged
under assets/licenses/phone-adb/). Upstream source archives for the native runtime, their SHA-256
checksums, pinned commits, local patches and build steps are listed in
third_party/native-runtime/provenance.json and runtime_tools/runtime_sources.lock.json. Local
patches are in runtime_tools/patches/ and the build steps are in
scripts/build_android_runtime_native.py.

